  "body": "fork synced at v0.16.0\n\n## What changed\n- Added rule in `AGENTS.md` under the \"Everything Is a Command\" section requiring that any PR adding a new user-facing command also introduces its MCP tool (and script verb where applicable) in `crates/app/src/mcp/`, or files a `source:agent` follow-up issue `MCP: <command>` and names it in the PR body.\n- Authored `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md` detailing the complete headless agent workflow (`import/open → set_stock → add_setup/set_wcs → add_fixture → add_tool → add_operation/list_features/set_operation_geometry → generate → verify/render_stock → post`), parameter DTO shapes, error/refusal structures (`isError: true`), and invariants.\n- Recorded decision ledger in `docs/decisions/356-commands-mcp-process.md`.\n\n## Readings & Gate\n- Quick gate (`scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick`): passed (0 failures, no crate code touched).\n- MCP test suite (`cargo test -p camcraft-app --test mcp`): 13/13 passed.\n- Workspace check (`cargo check --workspace`): clean compile.\n\n## Pinning tests\n- `mcp::handshake_and_tool_list`\n- `mcp::a_whole_job_over_the_tools`\n- `mcp::tool_library_export_import_roundtrip_into_a_fresh_document`\n- `mcp::detect_holes_fills_a_drill_from_its_model_and_undo_empties_it`\n\n## Not exercised\n- Live MCP WebSocket / socket server mode (#183 / #567, separate live session feature).\n\nChangelog: none (process and documentation only)\n\nFixes #356\n",
